ta/redis/.gitkeep   |   0\n data/redis/redis.conf |   9 +++\n data/run/.gitkeep     |   0\n requirements.txt      |   5 ++\n server/__init__.py    |   1 +\n server/app.py         |  55 +++++++++++++\n server/db.py          |  45 +++++++++++\n server/settings.py    |  86 ++++++++++++++++++++\n start.sh              | 217 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n tests/__init__.py     |   0\n tests/test_health.py  |  86 ++++++++++++++++++++\n 13 files changed, 519 insertions(+)\nstart.sh executable: yes\n6238 timeout 1200 loom lead --backend cursor --prompt /installed-agent/loom-marathon/prompts-generic/critic.md --message REVIEW CONTRACT task=MARATHON-2 attempt=1 base=585944254f44b8b0b4a9b891ea1dafb0d1764f7e candidate=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24  DESIGN: # MARATHON-2 ??? Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis  ## Summary  This task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.  ## Technical Approach  ### Decision  | Concern | Choice | |--------|--------| | Language / HTTP framework | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn** | | Shared durable store | **SQLite file** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` with **WAL** + busy timeout (shared by all nodes) | | Cross-node transport | **Local Redis** on `127.0.0.1:6379` (pub/sub / coordination only ??? **not** source of truth) | | Process supervisor | **`/app/start.sh`** (bash): create dirs, ensure venv+deps, start Redis + 3 Uvicorn workers, foreground wait loop with respawn | | Runtime root | Repo root **is** `/app` when the verifier runs |  ### Why this stack  - Epic/instruction leave language open; Python 3.12, `sqlite3`, and `redis-server` are already on the image. FastAPI covers REST + future WebSockets (Starlette) without a second runtime for the backend/IRC path. - Redis outage requirements (MARATHON-14: writes and dense `seq` continue while Redis is dead) **forbid** using Redis as the durable store. SQLite on a shared filesystem path is the simplest self-contained SoT that all three processes can open. - A shell supervisor matches the verifier contract (`./start.sh` foreground) and can respawn both HTTP and Redis without DinD or external orchestrators.  ### Alternatives considered  | Alternative | Rejected because | |------------|------------------| | Node.js + Express/Fastify | Equally viable for HTTP/WS; would split backend (IRC later) across languages or force Node for IRC too. Python keeps one backend language. | | Redis as primary DB | Contradicts Redis-`SIGKILL` resilience (writes must succeed without Redis). | | Postgres / Docker services | Remote/DinD-ish; not self-contained on this image. | | One process binding three ports | Harder crash isolation; grader kills **one** node and expects the other two to keep serving ??? three OS processes are required. | | Systemd / supervisord | Extra dependency; bash loop is enough and stays in-repo. |  ### Trade-off accepted  SQLite WAL under concurrent writers is correct for this density but needs disciplined `busy_timeout` / short transactions in later tasks. We accept that complexity over introducing another datastore. Dependency install on first boot (`pip install -r requirements.txt` into `/app/.venv`) adds a few seconds to cold start ??? acceptable vs baking undeclared global packages into the image.  ### Conventions fixed for sibling tasks (no sibling designs exist yet)  1. Product name: **Huddle**. 2. API prefix: `/api/...`; JSON; REST status codes per epic instruction. 3. `node_id` ??? `{0,1,2}` ??? ports `{8000,8001,8002}` (never swap). 4. Durable SoT: SQLite under `/app/data/`; Redis is ephemeral fan-out only. 5. Health response is **not** resource-enveloped (explicit epic exception): `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}`. 6. Env per process: `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` (default `/app/data`), `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` (default `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`).  ## Interface Contracts  ### Seam: Verifier / browser ??? HTTP nodes  #### `GET /api/health`  | Side | Responsibility | |------|----------------| | **Server (each node)** | Return `200` with `Content-Type: application/json` body exactly shaped as below. Does **not** require auth. Does **not** need to probe Redis or SQLite for this task (liveness of the HTTP process is enough). | | **Client / grader** | `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{N}/api/health` and assert sta  You are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line: REVIEW attempt=1 commit=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24 APPROVED ??? <reason> or REVIEW attempt=1 commit=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24 CHANGES-REQUESTED ??? <reason>\n6239 loom lead --backend cursor --prompt /installed-agent/loom-marathon/prompts-generic/critic.md --message REVIEW CONTRACT task=MARATHON-2 attempt=1 base=585944254f44b8b0b4a9b891ea1dafb0d1764f7e candidate=fba2eb628deb2875e1217dab3fbfeaec3179ae24  DESIGN: # MARATHON-2 ??? Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis  ## Summary  This task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared